From 30ff426abb0c99d754eb3629d69506ff27e1c61e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel <kernel@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:33:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ik2: Q4_K / Q5_0 experts (AtomicChat
 Inkling-2-Mini-Uncensored-AD-Q4_K)

- src/ik2/ik2_kq.h: ggml's Q4_K / Q5_0 values and one fixed row-dot order (units, explicit FMAs, exact plain
  products) shared by host and device; row_dot_host emulates the warp.
- ik2_kernels.cu: decode_value / block_values / block_bytes, fast decode_f16 kernels, row_dot / row_dot_2 /
  row_dot_multi / row_dot_pair_multi cases; register kernels experts_q4k_gu / experts_q50_down (AMD IK2_HIP_EXPV=1,
  IK2_HIP_NT bit 1 non-temporal; CUDA IK2_EXPV_KQ=1 for tests) with the shared-memory kernels' bits.
- ik2_rdna.inc: prompt WMMA tiles for Q4_K gate/up and Q5_0 down (mixed types per layer).
- ik2_main.cu: a row is whole blocks per role (gate/up: C, down: F).
- CUDA-only shim for the hipx14 AMD builtins so ik2_kernels.cu builds under nvcc again.
- tests: ik2_kq_test (host, vs ggml), ik2_kernels_test Q4_K / Q5_0 cases and bit-exact checks.
